OpenJarvis was developed at Hazy Research and the Scaling Intelligence Lab at
Stanford SAIL, as part of the Intelligence Per Watt research initiative. The
five-primitive architecture, the energy-aware evaluation harness and the
trace-driven learning loop originate there.

Nira is an independent fork. It is not a Stanford project, is not affiliated
with Hazy Research, the Scaling Intelligence Lab, Stanford SAIL or Intelligence
Per Watt, and is not endorsed by them. Its sponsors, if any, are its own; the
organisations that support the upstream project do not support this fork.

Files modified from the original carry no separate marker; the divergence is
recorded in the commit history and summarised in PLAN.md.

